issues.body:
The thread that is started here line 96, WebSocketClient.java

  public void connect() {
   (new Thread(this)).start();
  }

Never exits the run() function.

Calling close does disconnect the websocket and call the onClose function, however the thread just sits on the selector.select(); call.

Socket.IO server (http://github.com/learnboost/socket.io-node) uses a path part of the URI to identify connections.

Currently net.tootallnate.websocket.WebSocketClient#run() handles the path like this
    String path = "/" + uri.getPath();
which, if the specified server URI is for example ws://127.0.0.1/socket.io/websocket, results in path being //socket.io/websocket, which is not recognized by Socket.IO server.

Fix:
    String path = uri.getPath() == "" ? "/" : uri.getPath();

