I recently figured out a problem that had been plaguing us for a while: the server would sporadically send disconnect messages, and we'd lose a message.  I finally figured out that when the server sent the client a message, it reset its ping timer, but not the timeout on a pong message from the client.  Now, it seems like some websockets implementations send pong messages at will or in response to some text messages, but Java-WebSocket doesn't - as is acceptable under the current specifications.
However, when multiple messages were sent over the course of 100 seconds, the server never sent any ping messages, and thus never got any pong messages.  The server therefore disconnected the client.  To anyone experiencing similar symptoms, I recommend sending a pong message on receiving a text message, perhaps if a certain amount of time has elapsed since the last pong.  To send a pong, one can use (in their implementation of WebSocketClient):

```
                FramedataImpl1 pong = new FramedataImpl1( Opcode.PONG );
                pong.setFin(false);
                this.sendFrame(pong);
```

I don't know if the setFin is required, but I put it in just in case.

